{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-45616-r4515344","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Vanilla Crisps","sourcePageId":45616,"sourceRevision":"4515344","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T03:08:51Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Vanilla%20Crisps&oldid=4515344","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:29:16.734Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cookies","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using vanilla","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"25275c49f3a0f7d8e1804a137164fa66bf37a7609edc8a26d6e2ba6998d6dd10","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cookie recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nA '''vanilla crisp''' is a tasty cookie that is much like a sugar cookie, but takes less time to make.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Shortening|shortening]]\n*⅔ cup white [[Cookbook:Granulated Sugar|granulated sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*2 ½ cups [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 375°[[Cookbook:F|F]].\n# [[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] butter, shortening and sugar together.\n# Add salt and vanilla.\n# One at a time, [[Cookbook:Beating|beat]] eggs into mixture.\n# Stir flour into mixture to make [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]].\n# Roll dough into small balls and press into circular shapes on ungreased [[Cookbook:Baking Sheet|cookie sheet]].\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 8–10 minutes.\n# Remove immediately from pan and allow to cool.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Unlike sugar cookies, there is no need to chill before baking.\n* To give an extra taste, add 1 teaspoon of [[Cookbook:Almond Extract|almond extract]].\n\n[[Category:Recipes for cookies]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vanilla]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Vanilla Crisps","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup butter or margarine","sourceText":"½ cup butter or margarine","amountText":"½ cup butter or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup shortening","sourceText":"½ cup shortening","amountText":"½ cup shortening","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"⅔ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"⅔ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"⅔ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 teaspoon salt","sourceText":"1 teaspoon salt","amountText":"1 teaspoon salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 teaspoons vanilla","sourceText":"2 teaspoons vanilla","amountText":"2 teaspoons vanilla","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 ½ cups all-purpose flour","sourceText":"2 ½ cups all-purpose flour","amountText":"2 ½ cups all-purpose flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Preheat oven to 375°F.","sourceText":"Preheat oven to 375°F.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Cream butter, shortening and sugar together.","sourceText":"Cream butter, shortening and sugar together.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Add salt and vanilla.","sourceText":"Add salt and vanilla.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"One at a time, beat eggs into mixture.","sourceText":"One at a time, beat eggs into mixture.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Stir flour into mixture to make dough.","sourceText":"Stir flour into mixture to make dough.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Roll dough into small balls and press into circular shapes on ungreased cookie sheet.","sourceText":"Roll dough into small balls and press into circular shapes on ungreased cookie sheet.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Bake for 8–10 minutes.","sourceText":"Bake for 8–10 minutes.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":8,"text":"Remove immediately from pan and allow to cool.","sourceText":"Remove immediately from pan and allow to cool.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."